<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n108627" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπο-κρῐτικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>belonging to</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπόκρισις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11
				</span></i>
			, <i>skilled therein,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔστι φύσεως τὸ ὑ. εἶναι</span>”
				<i>having a good delivery,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					1404a15
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>suited for speaking</i> or <i>delivery,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λέξις -κωτάτη</span> ib. <i><span class="en">
				1413b9
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Demetr.
				<u>Eloc.</u>
				193
			</span></i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ -κή</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέχνη</span>) <i>the art of delivery,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1404a13
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Po.</u>
				1456b10
			</span></i>, al. (but, <i>the actor's art,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Vict.</u>
				1.24
			</span></i> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑποκριταί</span>
			), <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Mus.</u>
				p.91
			</span></i> K., <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				<u>Thras.</u>
				27
			</span></i>). Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Chamael.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				9.407a
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> metaph.,
				<i>acting a part, pretending to,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑ. τοῦ βελτίονος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Alex.</u>
					4
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Vett.Val.
				42.25
			</span></i>, al. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					38.19
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
